  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a full set at The Caverns in Pelham, Tennessee, on Sunday, April 21, 2024 [1][3]. This concert is the 421st of 467 archived shows for the band, following a previous appearance at the Gothic Theatre on April 17, 2024 [2]. The recommended recording, captured by astrolyric, is an audience tape lasting 108 minutes that includes 22 songs [1]. The setlist opens with “Azo Tle Nelli In Tlalticpac?” and “Sicilian Crest” before moving into tracks from albums like *Bleed Out* and *Jenny from Thebes* [1]. Notable rare performances include “Extraction Point,” “Bell Swamp Connection,” and “Only Takes a Few” [1]. A highlight is “Dark as a Dungeon,” a Merle Travis cover that had not been played in 582 days, making it a bustout in the archive [1][2]. The band also performed “In Memory of Satan” and “Woke Up New” [1]. The show concludes with a four-song encore featuring “Tidal Wave,” “Incandescent Ruins,” “Cotton,” and “Up The Wolves” [1]. The uploader notes the recording is older and admits to less technical polish, describing it as having a brief warble [1]. A poster for the event is credited to panetory.com [3].",
